msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks recipes for brewing mead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks recipes for bronze and bronze goods."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks recipes for iron and iron goods.\nUnlocks the bloomery."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks recipes for making jewelry out of metals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks salt extraction in salt deposits (on the surface of salt lakes and in salt mines) and the salt pond."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks the ability to find and gather native metals.\nUnlocks metal ores (gold, silver, copper) and metalloids (antimony and arsenic).\nAllows you to build the forge."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks the ability to grow water-loving crops: rice and taro.\nAllows farms and plantations to pass fresh water along a chain (up to 3 hexes).\nAllows you to drain marshes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks the use of draft animals to turn millstones."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.description"
msgid "Unlocks the use of the water wheel to set millstones in motion."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "A plow yoked to oxen made it possible to work heavy soils and raised yields."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "A protoscience of attempts to turn base metals into gold."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Ancient civilizations could count, but only now has knowledge moved from simple recipes to strict proofs. Geometry and abstract calculation let people not just watch the world but compute it: from the shape of a wheel's teeth to the motion of the stars."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Bitumen became an important material for waterproofing, and for making glue and fuel."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Burning limestone in kilns made lime possible, a key building material and an ingredient for making cement."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "By mixing fat with lye, people got soap, the first step toward hygiene and medicine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Canals let people manage water flows, improving irrigation and opening new routes for trade."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Cheese kept milk for months, becoming an important winter supply."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Clay tablets became the first carrier of information, letting people pass knowledge across the centuries."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Draft animals let people harness animal strength for heavy work, greatly raising output and efficiency in farming and construction."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Dyeing cloth and pottery with various dyes is one of the oldest crafts."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Fermentation let people turn grain and fruit into alcohol, drunk in rituals and in daily life."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Fired clay became humanity's first artificial material, letting people store grain and water."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Fishing is one of humanity's oldest trades, and the first way to take food from the water."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "For centuries potters watched sand and alkali turn in their kilns into a shining crust of glass. Then one day someone had the idea of doing it on purpose. Glassmaking became more than an accident: it became a deliberate craft. The new material changed the world: beads, amulets, and later tableware and windows. Transparency became a symbol of enlightenment."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "In scriptoriums scribes copied, translated, rewrote and recensioned texts on administration, the worship of the gods, magic and the curing of disease."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Managing water flows became the key to claiming new lands: irrigation did more than water the fields, it drained waterlogged ground and turned marshes into fertile plains."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Mastering metals revolutionized the crafts: copper tools were tougher than stone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Mead is the oldest alcohol, brewed from honey and water."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Parchment became an important carrier of information in the ancient world."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People have tracked the turning of the seasons since the earliest times, but only now has the calendar become a standard tool of management: precise planning of sowing, pruning and harvest let plantations reach their full potential."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People learned to alloy copper with tin to make bronze, a hard metal for tools and weapons. Bronze became a key material for crafts and warfare."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People learned to draw stone and ore from the depths of the earth, opening a new era in tools."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People learned to find and use native metals, which occur in nature in pure form, with no need to smelt them out of ore."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People learned to tame bees for honey and wax, the only natural sweeteners and the stuff of candles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "People noticed that the white crust on the shores of salt lakes cleanses and bleaches wonderfully. So began the extraction of soda, a valuable mineral without which neither glassmaking nor soapmaking is possible."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Plantations made it possible to grow olives and citrus in bulk, providing valuable goods and oils."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Ropes became an important material for building, sailing and farming, letting people bind, haul and hoist loads."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Salt became an important product for preserving food."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Silk became a valuable material for clothing and trade, opening new possibilities for crafts and the economy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Taming animals gave people a steady source of meat, milk and hides."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Tanning gave people a tough, flexible material for clothing, footwear and gear."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The art of exploring the land and drawing maps of it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The first farmers noticed that seeds thrown into the ground grew again. Thus began the age of settled life."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The grape is one of the oldest crops, from which people learned to make wine, a drink for feasts and rituals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The idea of value and exchange led to money, the basis of trade and city growth."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The loom turned wool and flax into cloth, from which clothes were sewn."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The skill of laying stone made it possible to build sturdy buildings that outlived centuries."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The water wheel became an important source of power in the ancient world, automating the processing of grain and other materials."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "The wheel is one of humanity's greatest inventions, and it changed trade and war."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "This revolutionary invention made it possible to create an affordable, practical material for writing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Vegetable oil became an important food and a source of light."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Wine was made from grapes: it was a drink for feasts and rituals, and it also kept the perishable grapes from spoiling."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Wood is the oldest building material, and with the first axes people learned to fell trees and saw the trunks into planks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "technologies.flavor"
msgid "Working precious stones and metals turned the craft into art."
msgstr ""

